{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner bounded reading of R3 candidate49e6321eaae56c3f23b884c9bd2a0cd5194bdbdc: all155 added lines of its new correction section; main3.1,3.5,3.6,3.7,4.3,4.4 and5.2–5.8 in full. These are not the entire1,574-addition/35-deletion two-file diff, the entire4,450-line main, or ordinary approval. The unchanged facts companion keeps SHA25612db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0. All three exact-head subjects remain under ordinary review b9a18b1b/3a70e5a3, with no narrowing or planner adoption.\n\nThe proposed user policy preserves the requested continuity: disconnect alone does not revoke; A's device retirement leaves P's active B and hosted work able to continue. Last-controller-key loss, member removal or agent-key revocation stops new tools/push forwarding within the proposed60-second observation window, preserves the last acknowledged checkpoint and leaves prior effects to reconciliation. Recovery requires an explicit resume; removal never silently restores the old member. Holds do not instantly end on key revocation: renewal is refused and expiry/cancellation ends them; a pre-fence or old-token push can remain unknown at its old fork. Existing300/60/10-second and clock-dependent80-second boundaries are proposals, not measured unconditional outcomes. A person-held runtime's standing-check form is explicitly an owned gap. Credentials/signers remain outside the coding environment and model; renewal keeps the token, replacement is a separately recorded mint and gateway handoff, and unconfirmed revocations stay owed. Host-account compromise has operator obligations outside the scope ledger. Retention covers complete files/Git closure/conversation/command outcomes, seven-day configurable private retention, pins for unknown effects, tombstones and durable owned deletion.\n\nMember-authored prose is data rather than admitted control: titles/comments/terms/labels/results cannot grant authority. This addresses M6 as a distinct boundary; device-authority witness O4 alone cannot prove it. Invitations authenticate their secret before exposing used/expiry state, preserve a valid invitation under a refused limit attempt, and isolate join work from revocation/removal; redemption when served is not an unconditional timely-admission guarantee under arbitrary load. Secret-strength minima remain proposed.\n\nSections5.7/5.8 disclose real remaining seams rather than pretending delivery: read-decided publication versus individually unknown attempts O11, known-token expiry evidence O12, and unbounded retry-chain capacity O13; job dispatch/read-token ownership, bounded task notices, staged-ref snapshot size and result-details custody still need decisions. This candidate explicitly uses R1v9ba556 forms. R1v10f525 is now the current unadopted proposal and changes whole-duty closure and written-refusal accounting: reconcile actual sibling forms/reservations and all139 source choices before dependent delivery. Finite reservations must preserve unknown duties, not invent their settlement or silently remove required browser/workspace/device outcomes. Preserve the full R1/R3/R4 and I1 ownership, normal reviews and builder-judged Jam readiness; no new test engine, standalone gate or extra Jam prerequisite is requested.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}